SUMMARY:NJYC: Spring Concert
DESCRIPTION:NJYC: Spring Concert\nMay 17\, 2026 at 4:00 p.m.\n$20/Adults\, $15/Students & Seniors\nNicholas Music Center at Rutgers University\, New Brunswick\nClick HERE for tickets\nPlease use the link below to access the parking registration: https://www.masongross.rutgers.edu/events-tickets/plan-visit/  | Open the link and scroll down to [parking]. Click on [parking] and then [April 2026 Parking before 6 p.m. on weekdays].  You’ll be able to park in Lot 79\, Lot 74a or the Douglass Parking Deck.   \nNJYC Primo Coro\, Coriste: Trish Joyce\, Director\nNJYC Cor Amici\, Camerata: Dan Malloy\, Director\nNJYC Sola Voce: Joanna Scarangello\, Director\nAccompanists: Phillip Steffani\, Andrew Macirowski\, and Leah Frank \nCelebrate spring with the New Jersey Youth Chorus as our young singers bring a fresh\, uplifting program to life. Featuring a mix of classical and contemporary repertoire\, this concert reflects the season’s spirit of growth\, joy\, and shared musical expression.
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/spring-concert/
LOCATION:Nicholas Music Center at Rutgers New Brunswick\, 85 George St\, New Brunswick\, NJ\, 08901\, United States
CATEGORIES:NJYC,Wharton
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://whartonarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/i-2D7B824-X4.jpeg
END:VEVENT
