SUMMARY:Instrument Petting Zoo
DESCRIPTION:Instrument Petting Zoo\nFor Ages 4-7\nSaturday\, May 9\n10:30 a.m. – 12:30 p.m.\nFREE Event\nPerforming Arts School Front Lawn\n60 Locust Avenue\, Berkeley Heights \nThis is a relaxed\, hands-on event where young children can:\n🎶 Try a variety of instruments (violin\, winds\, percussion\, and more)\n🎶 Explore rhythm and movement through guided activities\n🎶 Build comfort and curiosity around music in a playful setting\n🎶 Meet our faculty and staff \nQuestions? Call (908) 790-0700 or email info@whartonarts.org.
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/instrument-petting-zoo/
LOCATION:Wharton Institute for the Performing Arts\, 60 Locust Avenue\, Berkeley Heights\, NJ\, 07922\, United States
CATEGORIES:PAS,PAS Current Students,Wharton
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://whartonarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Summer-Camp-Illustration-Exploration-of-Instruments-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
